    "view": {
      "value": "<p>If you want to analyse a database, understand relations between its tables etc., you can use this tool : <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://schemaspy.sourceforge.net/\" rel=\"nofollow\">schemaspy</a></p><p>Example usage:</p><h2 id=\"Generatingdatabasediagramsforschemaanalysis-Creatingopenerpdatabasediagrams\">Creating openerp database diagrams</h2><ol><li>Download schemaspy from : <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://sourceforge.net/projects/schemaspy/files/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://sourceforge.net/projects/schemaspy/files/</a></li><li>It used to have dependency on Graphviz, so you may also have to install graphviz : <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://www.graphviz.org/Download..php\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://www.graphviz.org/Download..php</a></li><li>command to execute the jar :<br/><p>java -jar schemaSpy_5.0.0.jar -t pgsql  -db openerp -s public -u openerp -p &lt;password&gt; -host &lt;host&gt; -o &lt;output dir&gt; -dp &lt;path-to-the-db-driver&gt;</p></li></ol><p>More info on the parameters can be found at <a class=\"external-link\" href=\"http://schemaspy.sourceforge.net/\" rel=\"nofollow\">http://schemaspy.sourceforge.net/</a></p><p> </p><p> </p><p> </p><div class=\"confluence-information-macro confluence-information-macro-information conf-macro output-block\" data-hasbody=\"true\" data-macro-id=\"\" data-macro-name=\"info\"><span class=\"aui-icon aui-icon-small aui-iconfont-info confluence-information-macro-icon\"> </span><div class=\"confluence-information-macro-body\"> </div></div><h2 id=\"Generatingdatabasediagramsforschemaanalysis-Relatedarticles\">Related articles</h2><p></p><p>\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    \n    <ul class=\"content-by-label conf-macro output-block\" data-hasbody=\"false\" data-macro-id=\"\" data-macro-name=\"contentbylabel\">\n        <li>\n        <div>\n                <span class=\"icon aui-icon content-type-page\" title=\"Page\">Page:</span>        </div>\n\n        <div class=\"details\">\n          